<http://data.silknow.org/object/faf946bb-3c3f-3b43-85f0-5767b11ce30d>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Textile hanging of linen and silk. Coarse and unbleached linen ground woven with a large scale symmetrical pattern of curving leaves with lattice fillings. This is formed by a pattern weft of low grade silk in light brown, bound in tabby with a very thin and tightly spun binding warp of silk. The material was originally 24 inches wide and a strip has been added to either side to make it a curtain. A plain fringe also in brown silk has been added at the top end of the pattern. The material was woven on a draw loom. Tissue - the binding warp is interwoven with the ground weft."@en , "Textile hanging of linen and silk, Italy, 1750-1799"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/634ad4e4-ea47-3dcd-bf4f-173b8dd0e09a> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Textile hanging of linen and silk. Coarse and unbleached linen ground woven with a large scale symmetrical pattern of curving leaves with lattice fillings. This is formed by a pattern weft of low grade silk in light brown, bound in tabby with a very thin and tightly spun binding warp of silk. The material was originally 24 inches wide and a strip has been added to either side to make it a curtain. A plain fringe also in brown silk has been added at the top end of the pattern. The material was woven on a draw loom. Tissue - the binding warp is interwoven with the ground weft."@en , "Textile hanging of linen and silk, Italy, 1750-1799"@en ;
